{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>All the vessels of the Tabernacle.</b> That were needed for its erection and its dismantling — such as mallets to drive the pegs and the pillars." "<b>Pegs.</b> A kind of copper stakes made for the tent curtains and for the hangings of the court, tied with cords all around at their lower edges, so that the wind would not lift them. And I do not know whether they were driven into the ground, or tied and suspended, their weight holding down the lower edges of the curtains so they would not move in the wind. And I say that Scripture testifies about them that they are driven into the ground — therefore they are called pegs. And this verse supports me: ״אֹהֶל בַּל יִצְעָן בַּל יִסַּע יְתֵדֹתָיו לָנֶצַח״ (Isaiah 33)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:00.931537382Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}